# Who may sign release tags (daemon/v*, app/v*, plugin/v*): OpenSSH allowed_signers format, see
# "ALLOWED SIGNERS" in ssh-keygen(1). daemon/scripts/release.sh and sign-release.sh check every
# release tag with `git verify-tag` against this file as of the previous release tag, so a signer
# added here becomes trusted only from the release after the one that ships this change
# (daemon/docs/release.md, "Signed Tags"). The file is under CODEOWNERS.
#
# One line per key: <principal> namespaces="git" <key type> <public key>
# The key is the maintainer's SSH key on a hardware token, with a touch for every signature:
#   ssh-keygen -t ed25519-sk -O resident -O verify-required -C wardenclaw-release-tags
# Example line (not a real key):
#   maintainer@users.noreply.github.com namespaces="git" sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com AAAAGnNrLXNzaC1lZDI1NTE5QG9wZW5zc2guY29tAAAA...
